        },
        "subject": "LU-20637 lfs: grow -printf over a target as a walk does",
        "message": "LU-20637 lfs: grow -printf over a target as a walk does\n\nlfs find --device -printf keeps its output in pieces until each\npathname is known.  The pieces were built in a fixed 1024-byte\nbuffer and kept in a 2048-byte blob, so a format with %LO for a wide\nor overstriped file lost the rest of its line, newline included, and\nthe next match ran on.  A walk grows its buffer up to\nFORMATTED_BUF_MAX.  Grow the target scan's buffers the same way.\n\nconf-sanity 307 compares a walk and a target scan over an\noverstriped file.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=307\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7d52824b19c5954ce4d4c9b53cb0ebe3ba277fd6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
